VALUES ('honda', 'pilot', 'cargo-space', $s$Honda$s$, $s$Pilot$s$, $s$Cargo space$s$, $s$Honda Pilot Cargo Space: 18.6 cu ft, up to 87.0 Behind Row One (2026)$s$, $s$Honda Pilot Cargo Space: 18.6 to 87.0 cu ft (2026)$s$, $s$Honda Pilot cargo space from Honda's 2026 specification sheet: 18.6 cu ft behind the third row, 48.5 behind the second and 87.0 behind the first.$s$, $s$[{"q": "How much cargo space does a 2026 Honda Pilot have?", "a": "18.6 cu ft behind the third row, 48.5 cu ft behind the second row and 87.0 cu ft behind the first row on most trims, by Honda's 2026 sheet. Elite and Black Edition are listed at 86.5 cu ft behind the first row."}, {"q": "Why does Honda print two cargo figures for each row?", "a": "Honda lists a standard figure and a maximum figure. Its footnote says the measurement follows the SAE J1100 standard plus, where applicable, floor space between seating rows with the seats in their forward-most and upright position."}, {"q": "Which Pilot trim has the most cargo room?", "a": "On the maximum figure behind the first row, the TrailSport is highest at 113.7 cu ft."}]$s$::jsonb, $s${"answer": "The 2026 Honda Pilot has 18.6 cu ft of cargo volume behind the third row, 48.5 cu ft behind the second row and 87.0 cu ft behind the first row (86.5 on Elite and Black Edition), according to Honda's specification sheet. Honda also prints a larger maximum figure for each row.", "covers": "Model year 2026", "not_covered": "2023 to 2025 and earlier generations: Honda's figures for those years are not on this page yet.", "sections": [{"id": "cargo", "h": "Cargo volume by trim, standard / maximum (2026)", "table": {"head": ["Trim", "Behind third row", "Behind second row", "Behind first row"], "rows": [["Sport", "18.6 / 21.8 cu ft", "48.5 / 59.5 cu ft", "87.0 / 111.8 cu ft", 1], ["EX-L", "18.6 / 22.4 cu ft", "48.5 / 60.1 cu ft", "87.0 / 112.4 cu ft", 1], ["TrailSport", "18.6 / 21.8 cu ft", "48.5 / 59.5 cu ft", "87.0 / 113.7 cu ft", 1], ["Touring", "18.6 / 22.4 cu ft", "48.5 / 60.1 cu ft", "87.0 / 112.4 cu ft", 1], ["Elite", "18.6 / 22.4 cu ft", "48.5 / 60.1 cu ft", "86.5 / 112.1 cu ft", 1], ["Black Edition", "18.6 / 22.4 cu ft", "48.5 / 60.1 cu ft", "86.5 / 112.1 cu ft", 1]]}, "notes": ["Honda's footnotes: based on the SAE J1100 cargo volume measurement standard; and the same standard plus, where applicable, floor space between seating rows and seats in their forward-most and upright position."]}], "check": ["The larger figures need seats folded or moved forward; with every seat in use you have the third-row figure.", "For a cargo box or a roof rack, the roof load limit matters, not the interior volume; look it up in your owner's manual.", "Always secure cargo and keep the total of passengers and cargo under the figure on the door jamb label.", "Your owner's manual and the labels on your own vehicle override this page."], "related": ["cargo-boxes", "roof-racks", "floor-mats"], "sources": [["Honda Newsroom, 2026 Honda Pilot Specifications & Features (26 Jan 2026)", "https://hondanews.com/en-US/honda-automobiles/releases/release-14c469388b7fed5af247fc02e2009aa7-2026-honda-pilot-specifications-features"]], "reviewed": "2026-11-23"}$s$::jsonb, 'published', DATE '2026-11-25', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-11-25 10:00:00+06', 'model', '')
